# The Docker build context is the repo root, but the image only needs the
# Cargo manifests, the crate sources, the bundled assets, and the deploy
# config. Without this file, `docker build .` ships the ENTIRE tree —
# including target/ (tens of GB of compiled artifacts) and .git — to the
# BuildKit daemon on every build, which dominates wall-clock time and
# pressures Docker's build cache into evicting the cargo target/ mounts
# (forcing a full dependency recompile). Ignore everything, then re-include
# only what the Dockerfile's COPY steps actually use.
*

!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!build.rs
!index.html
!Trunk.toml
!style.css
!nginx.conf
!supervisord.conf
!entrypoint.sh
!public
!src
!assets

# Re-exclude build artifacts that the broad re-includes above would pull
# back in (e.g. a stray target/ inside src/ tooling, editor scratch).
**/target
**/*.swp
